<title>USA: IBM's Ricciardi to act as interim CFO.</title>
<headline>IBM's Ricciardi to act as interim CFO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp said Thursday that senior vice president and chief counsel Lawrence Ricciardi would assume the responsibilties of chief financial officer on an interim basis.</p>
<p>Earlier today Xerox Corp said G. Richard Thoman, IBM's CFO, would become Xerox's president and chief operating officer, making him the heir apparent to Xerox Chairman and CEO Paul Allaire.</p>
<p>An IBM spokesman said it was premature to say if Ricciardi would become IBM's permanent CFO. &quot;He has a lot of experience in financial matters,&quot; said the spokesman.</p>
</text>
